---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CHAPTERS, PARTS } from '../lib/chapters';

const writtenCount = CHAPTERS.filter((c) => c.written).length;
---
<Base>
  <div class="narrow">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="tagline">$ raft --everything<span class="cursor">▊</span></p>
    <h1>Distributed systems, from the <em>lost packet</em> up.</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      Clocks lie, networks drop messages, and "the server is down" is indistinguishable
      from "the server is slow". This course builds consensus from first principles —
      Lamport clocks, failure detectors, Raft, quorums — until distributed databases stop
      being sorcery.
    </p>
    <a class="cta" href="/chapters/01-two-generals/">Start Chapter 1 →</a>
  </section>

  <h2 class="section-title" id="how">How this works</h2>
  <p class="section-sub">Every chapter follows the same promise:</p>
  <div class="method-grid">
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3><span>01</span>Start below the abstraction</h3>
      <p>Before "use etcd", we answer "why is agreement hard at all?"</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3><span>02</span>Nothing is magic</h3>
      <p>Every protocol is messages between processes you can crash on purpose.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3><span>03</span>Build a toy version</h3>
      <p>Elections, replicated logs, hash rings — and a toy Raft in ~400 lines.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3><span>04</span>The papers become readable</h3>
      <p>After building it, the Raft paper reads like documentation of your own code.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-title" id="chapters">Chapters</h2>
  <p class="section-sub">
    {writtenCount} of {CHAPTERS.length} chapters fully written{writtenCount === CHAPTERS.length ? ' — every chapter, start to finish.' : ' — the rest are outlined and on the way.'}
  </p>
  {PARTS.map((part) => (
    <div>
      <p class="part-label">{part}</p>
      <div class="chapter-grid">
        {CHAPTERS.filter((c) => c.part === part).map((c) => (
          <a class="chapter-card" href={`/chapters/${c.slug}/`}>
            <span class="num">{String(c.order).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <span class="body">
              <span class="t">{c.title}</span>
              <span class="b">{c.blurb}</span>
            </span>
            <span class="status dim">{c.written ? '✅' : '📝'}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  ))}
  </div>
</Base>
